body:
@olive oil{15%ml}
@onion{1}, diced
@carrot{2}, sliced
@celery stalk{2}, sliced
@garlic clove{2}, minced
@chicken thigh{600%g}, bone-in
@chicken stock{1.5%l}
@bay leaf{1}
@thyme{2%sprig}
@salt{1%tsp}
@black pepper{0.5%tsp}
@egg noodle{150%g}
@parsley{10%g}, chopped

Heat @olive oil{} in a large pot over medium heat. Add @onion{}, @carrot{}, and @celery stalk{}; cook until softened. Stir in @garlic clove{} briefly.

Add @chicken thigh{}, @chicken stock{}, @bay leaf{}, @thyme{}, @salt{}, and @black pepper{}. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a gentle simmer. Cover and cook until the chicken is tender and reaches 74°C at its thickest point.

Remove the chicken. Add @egg noodle{} to the pot and cook until tender according to the package directions. Discard the chicken skin and bones, shred the meat, and return it to the pot. Remove the bay leaf and thyme stems, stir in @parsley{}, and adjust seasoning.
